# WorkOS on Cloudflare Workers

`@vesta-cx/utils/auth` has been retired.

All shared auth logic belongs in `@vesta-cx/auth`, using `workos-node` (including its `workerd` export) plus shared transport/runtime boundaries.

When touching existing auth flows:

- Add or update auth behavior in `@vesta-cx/auth`, not `packages/utils`.
- Keep Cloudflare Workers as a first-class runtime; do not assume Node-only auth helpers.
- Do not reintroduce thin fetch wrappers around WorkOS endpoints unless the shared auth package explicitly needs a transport seam for testing or retries.

## Cloudflare Adapter Typing Gotcha

Remove `/// <reference types="@sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare" />` from `app.d.ts` — it declares `Platform.env: unknown`. Define `App.Platform` manually; runtime types come from `worker-configuration.d.ts`.
